From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:40:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mxl862xx: add MxL86252 support and combo-port SerDes mux

Extend the MxL862xx DSA driver for the MxL86252 (five 2.5G PHYs)
variant used on the Bananapi BPI-R4 Pro and add combo-port support:
a devicetree-described SerDes lane mux (ds-mux) that switches a
switch SerDes between an SFP+ cage and an external 10G PHY, with an
SFP presence monitor selecting the active channel at runtime. Also
extends the CTP/flow/RMON/MMD API definitions used by the new port
paths and fixes host-command and phylink handling for the 10G ports.

Based on the MaxLinear driver files from the MediaTek SDK; original
copyrights and GPL-2.0 licensing preserved.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
